CHANGES IN VERSION 0.99.7
-------------------------

SIGNIFICANT USER-VISIBLE CHANGES

    o The package requires R >= 4.6.0 (was 4.5.0).

DOCUMENTATION

    o New section in the vignette on how JASPAR replaces the per-release data
      packages (JASPAR2022, JASPAR2024), with code to move from them.
    o New CITATION file: the package and the papers of the JASPAR 2022, 2024
      and 2026 releases.
    o The README explains how to install the package from Bioconductor.
    o Shorter Description in DESCRIPTION. BugReports points to the GitHub
      issues page.
    o These changes were written with Claude Code (Anthropic, model Claude
      Opus 5.5) under the direction of the maintainer; the new files state
      their provenance.

CHANGES IN VERSION 0.99.6
-------------------------

DOCUMENTATION

    o The code, tests and vignette written or rewritten in 0.99.5 now state
      their provenance, as the Bioconductor policy on AI-generated code asks:
      they were written with Claude Code (Anthropic, model Claude Sonnet 5.5)
      under the direction of the maintainer.

CHANGES IN VERSION 0.99.5
-------------------------

SIGNIFICANT USER-VISIBLE CHANGES

    o JASPAR() retrieves the JASPAR SQLite databases through AnnotationHub.
      Before, it downloaded them from the URL in inst/extdata/metadata.csv with
      BiocFileCache. The AnnotationHub record is chosen by version from the hub
      metadata. The package contains no accession numbers, so a release that
      is added to AnnotationHub, or whose record is corrected, can be
      retrieved without a new version of the package.
    o The default version of JASPAR() changed from "JASPAR2026" to
      "JASPAR2024", in the code, the help pages and the examples.
    o getAvailableJASPARVersions() lists the versions that are registered in
      AnnotationHub. Its argument 'package' is replaced by 'hub'.
    o New argument 'hub' of JASPAR(): an AnnotationHub object to use, for
      example AnnotationHub::AnnotationHub(localHub = TRUE) to work offline.
    o If a database cannot be retrieved, the error names the version and the
      AnnotationHub accession and gives the reason reported by AnnotationHub. A
      cached file that is not an SQLite database or is cut short is downloaded
      once more (not with a local hub, which cannot download).
    o The package no longer depends on BiocFileCache directly. It imports
      AnnotationHub.

NEW FEATURES

    o show() method for JASPAR objects.
    o The vignette follows the AnnotationHub workflow: query the hub, retrieve
      a version, and search it with TFBSTools.
    o Unit tests.
